{
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "id": "dropbear_ssh_repo",
  "name": "Dropbear SSH Repo",
  "description": "Standalone KPM repository for the dropbear-ssh package (on-demand SSH/SFTP over WiFi for jailbroken Kindles)",
  "packages": {
    "dropbear-ssh": {
      "name": "Dropbear SSH",
      "author": "Akshay",
      "description": "SSH and SFTP over your existing WiFi, no USB networking needed. Launching opens a status app with a Start/Stop button that shows the connect command and password while the server is running, a field for setting your own password, a Check for Update button, and a \"Keep reachable while Kindle sleeps\" option that defers the device's suspend cycle so the server stays reachable through sleep (costs battery, since WiFi and CPU stay up; the e-ink screen does not). The server keeps running after the app is closed. Buttons talk to a loopback-only bridge on the device, not to any external server. A random password is generated at install and printed in the KPM log; change it from the app or at /mnt/us/usbnetlite/etc/ssh_password. Verified on Paperwhite 4 (kernel 4.1.x), Paperwhite 5 (4.9.77), and Paperwhite 6 / V\u00e9ra (5.15.x). Ships two binary builds per upstream's release split, selected automatically by kernel version at install time. Repackaged from notmarek/kindle-usbnetlite.",
